PARITY (web KeyboardShortcutsModal.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
==================================================================================
  Data sources (web -> native P1/S8 seam):
    useTranslation   -> KBShortcutsStrings facade (P1/S10), no literals.
    useAllShortcuts  -> KBShortcutsSource pushes [KBShortcutEntry] (web registry snapshot).
    useLocation      -> KBShortcutsUpdate.pathname (drives the route gate); no router in view.
    useShortcut      -> registration is the producer side of the registry; the cheat sheet
                        is a pure CONSUMER, so the native source supplies the resolved
                        snapshot (the production adapter binds the shared registry holder).
  Logic (verbatim ports):
    mode 'all'|'global'|'page'             -> KBShortcutFilter (+ sessionStorage default 'all').
    filteredGroups scope/route/search       -> KBShortcutsProjection.isVisible (global drops
                                               non-global; page drops global; any non-global
                                               needs a matching routeMatch; description
                                               substring of the trimmed lowercased needle).
    routeMatch string startsWith / RegExp   -> KBShortcutRouteMatch .prefix (hasPrefix) /
                                               .regex (NSRegularExpression firstMatch).
    GROUP_PRIORITY + groupRank              -> first whitespace/'(' token, lowercased, mapped.
    group sort (rank desc, localeCompare)   -> groups() sorts rank desc then title asc;
                                               entries inside sorted by id (web a.id.localeCompare).
    FILTER_STORAGE_KEY + read/writeStored   -> KBShortcutsFilterStore (UserDefaults, same key).
    reset search on close (useEffect open)  -> model.resetSearch() on .onDisappear.
  Composition (web Modal/body -> native):
    Modal title + close "x"            -> KBShortcutHeader (title + freshness chip + close).
    SearchInput (debounced)            -> KBShortcutSearchField (magnifier + TextField +
                                          clear), verbatim prompt (per-surface i18n table
                                          can't resolve via the shared field's LocalizedStringKey).
    role=tablist All/Global/This page  -> KBShortcutFilterControl (capsule segmented chips,
                                          .isSelected a11y), built in-surface, exactly as the
                                          0017 sibling built its fields in-surface.
    grouped <section> + <h3>           -> KBShortcutList sections with a label title.
    row desc + <kbd> chips joined "+"  -> KBShortcutRow (desc + KBShortcutKeyCap chips with a
                                          "+" between).
    "No shortcuts match your search."  -> empty envelope (ContentUnavailableView).
  Native widening (honest, documented): the web component is prop-driven (open/onClose) over a
  synchronous in-memory store; the native surface widens it into the prompt-required loading /
  empty / error / stale / offline envelopes (a registry hydrated async / cross-pod), with a
  freshness chip + cached-data banner + one guarded stale auto-refresh. Tailwind classes were
  NOT ported; chrome is P1/S9 tokens (TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS/Font.TS) via TSGlassPanel/
  TSFadeIn.

==================================================================================
STATES (every state renders -- no hidden surfaces)
==================================================================================
  loading  -> KBShortcutLoadingState (spinner + "Loading shortcuts...") before first entries.
  empty    -> KBShortcutEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView, web "No shortcuts match your
              search.") -- covers both no-registered and no-match.
  error    -> KBShortcutErrorState (QueryError-equivalent + Retry -> model.refresh()).
  stale    -> freshness chip "Stale" + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh (re-armed
              on return to live).
  offline  -> freshness chip "Offline" + banner; cached snapshot kept; no refetch.
  content  -> the grouped list (filtered + grouped + rank/title sorted; per-group id-sorted rows).
  Telemetry: model.start() emits P1/S11 view.opened surface="KeyboardShortcutsModal" (once,
  idempotent -- ModelTests proven).

